Synthetic Wikimedia recent-changes events generated by Generate in this
package (seeded PCG), released under the repository licence. No real wiki
content, user names or IP addresses are included: titles come from small word
lists and IPs are from the documentation ranges (RFC 5737, RFC 3849).

Schema origin: field names and types follow the mediawiki/recentchange 1.0.1
event schema from Wikimedia's schemas-event-primary repository (Apache-2.0):
https://gitlab.wikimedia.org/repos/data-engineering/schemas-event-primary/-/blob/e3f4ba02593e471a361ceb0e2da312588c12bfd1/jsonschema/mediawiki/recentchange/1.0.1.yaml
Commit: e3f4ba02593e471a361ceb0e2da312588c12bfd1. The schema allows additional
properties; title_url, notify_url, topic, partition and offset are extra
fields the live stream emits.

Real events are not used: the EventStreams feed states no data licence (edit
summaries are user contributions, user names and IPs are personal data) and
there is no immutable archive to pin.

Regenerate sample.jsonl.zst with: go test ./datasets/wikirc -update
